0068 | 
0069 |   // ==== non-keyed reverse sorted(), concrete leg (v3) =======================
0070 |   // sort.k's condRev(sortVS(VS), true) reverses equal-key runs — invisible on
0071 |   // the all-Int / all-str lists sortVS used to accept, visible once sortVS
0072 |   // orders mixed numerics (CPython keeps FIRST-seen order among equal keys
0073 |   // under reverse=True). rev-in/rev-out over the same stable ascending sortVS
0074 |   // is exactly CPython's stable descending sort, and is output-identical on the
0075 |   // old homogeneous domains. krun-only (priority 40; proofs keep sort.k's
0076 |   // condRev(sortVS(VS), RB) term unchanged).
END 0067 rule
BEGIN 0077 rule attrs=priority
