0141 |   // ---- exact mixed Int/Float comparison ------------------------------------
0142 |   // The old rules compared via intToF(I), which ROUNDS ints >= 2^53 to a nearby
0143 |   // double (so e.g. 9007199254740993 > 9007199254740992.0 came out false). Compare
0144 |   // the REAL values instead: for a finite float F and an integer I,
0145 |   //     F <  I   <=>   floor(F) <  I
0146 |   //     F >  I   <=>   ceil(F)  >  I
0147 |   //     F == I   <=>   F is integral  AND  floor(F) == I
0148 |   // floorFloat/ceilFloat are exact and Float2Int yields the EXACT integer of an
0149 |   // integral float (no rounding), so this is exact for every finite F. Non-finite
0150 |   // F keeps the old intToF path (rounding is irrelevant to +/-inf and NaN, and
0151 |   // inf/NaN have no integer floor). Opaque for kprove, [concrete] for krun.
END 0139 rule
